# Compatibility shim — .trivyignore.yaml is the source of truth for rationale,
# package scoping (purls) and expiry. Keep the ID lists here in sync with it.
#
# This plain file exists because trivy auto-detects `.trivyignore` by filename
# but needs an explicit `--ignorefile` to load the YAML form. Our own workflow
# passes the flag, but this repo is also scanned as a submodule path by the
# baseapp-frontend-template Jenkins pipeline, whose trivy command we don't
# control (shared library `scanDependencyVulnerabilities`). Without this file
# that scan would lose the waivers.
#
# image-size: no patched release exists in any version line; reached only
# through metro (React Native bundler) at build time, never shipped in the app
# bundle. Re-evaluate by 2026-11-11.
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330
#
# node-forge: no patched release exists (advisory covers <= 1.4.0, the latest).
# Reached only through dev tooling — @expo/cli (dev-server code signing) and
# webpack-dev-server's selfsigned cert generator — never shipped in an app
# bundle. Re-evaluate by 2026-12-31.
CVE-2026-85393
